---
import Article from "../../layouts/Article.astro";
import { LAND_KM2 } from "../../data/leonida";

const MAPS = [
  { id: "gta6", name: "GTA 6 (Leonida)", km2: LAND_KM2, color: "#ff3d8b", note: "Land on the YANIS v18 community map, measured by HeistCalc" },
  { id: "rdr2", name: "Red Dead Redemption 2", km2: 75, color: "#ff9a3c", note: "Fan measurement, method unclear (2018)" },
  { id: "gta5land", name: "GTA V (land only)", km2: 49.6, color: "#4dd2ff", note: "Community land measurement (KrundstLord)" },
  { id: "gta5pop", name: "GTA V (popular figure)", km2: 75.8, color: "#2b8cff", note: "Widely quoted fan figure, unclear if water is included" },
  { id: "gta4", name: "GTA IV (Liberty City)", km2: 16.1, color: "#b9a7cc", note: "Fan figure, method unclear" },
];

const faq = [
  { q: "How big is the GTA 6 map in km²?", a: `Rockstar hasn't published a figure. Measured on the latest community map, Leonida has about ${LAND_KM2} km² of land, in line with other community land measurements of 83.8 to 85.6 km². Older estimates of 110 to 125 km² came from earlier, less accurate versions of the map.` },
  { q: "Is the GTA 6 map twice the size of GTA 5?", a: "That's what Rockstar has said. Measured land against land, it's closer to 1.7 times GTA V. The gap shrinks or grows depending on whether water, marshland and GTA V's own disputed size are counted." },
  { q: "Is GTA 6 bigger than Red Dead Redemption 2?", a: "Yes. Rockstar has called it about three times RDR2's map. Using a common fan figure of about 75 km² for RDR2, land measurements put Leonida only slightly larger, so Rockstar's comparison probably counts water and playable space differently." },
  { q: "How long is GTA 6's map from top to bottom?", a: "Roughly 16.6 km from the northern border to the southern Keys, and about 11.6 km west to east, measured on the community map." },
];
---
<Article
  title="GTA 6 Map Size: Leonida vs GTA 5 & RDR2 in km²"
  h1="How Big Is the GTA 6 Map? Leonida's Size Compared"
  description={`GTA 6's Leonida is about ${LAND_KM2} km² of land by our measurement. Compare it to GTA 5, RDR2 and GTA 4 to scale, and see why sites quote such different numbers.`}
  published="2026-11-18"
  crumbs={[{ href: "/gta-6/", label: "GTA 6" }, { href: "/gta-6/map/", label: "Map" }]}
  faq={faq}
  tool={{ name: "GTA 6 Map Size Comparison" }}
  sources={[
    { href: "https://mapheist.com/en/analysis/gta-6-map-size/", label: "mapheist: GTA 6 map size figures and Rockstar quotes compiled" },
    { href: "https://insider-gaming.com/gta-6-map-size/", label: "Insider Gaming: Rockstar on Leonida's size (via Edge)" },
    { href: "https://www.dexerto.com/gta/rockstar-says-gta-6s-map-is-so-big-you-wont-see-it-all-just-by-playing-story-missions-3414118/", label: "Dexerto: Rockstar repeats \"twice GTA 5\"" },
    { href: "https://map.gtadb.org", label: "gtadb.org: YANIS v18 community map tiles (CC BY 4.0)" },
  ]}
>
  <section slot="tool" class="calc" id="size-tool">
    <h2>Compare to scale</h2>
    <div class="size-picks" role="group" aria-label="Maps to compare">
      {MAPS.map((m) => (
        <label class="size-pick"><input type="checkbox" value={m.id} checked={m.id === "gta6" || m.id === "gta5land" || m.id === "rdr2"} /> <span style={`--c:${m.color}`}>{m.name}</span></label>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="size-stage" aria-hidden="true"><div class="size-squares" id="size-squares"></div></div>
    <div class="table-scroll"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Map</th><th class="num">Land area</th><th class="num">GTA 6 is</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody id="size-rows"></tbody>
    </table></div>
    <p class="muted-sm">Squares are drawn to scale by area. Shapes are simplified, since every map has its own outline.</p>
  </section>

  <p><strong>Leonida has about {LAND_KM2} km² of land</strong>, measured on the latest community map. That makes it Rockstar's biggest world, though by less than "twice GTA V" suggests if you only count dry land. It stretches about 16.6 km north to south and 11.6 km east to west.</p>

  <h2>What Rockstar has said</h2>
  <p>Rockstar hasn't given a figure in square kilometres. Its comparisons, as reported in interviews:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>About twice the size of GTA V's map.</strong> Repeated by Rockstar developers in several interviews, including Aaron Garbut to Game Informer.</li>
    <li><strong>About three times Red Dead Redemption 2's map.</strong> Reported from Rob Nelson's comments to creators in August.</li>
    <li><strong>Close to GTA IV, GTA V and RDR2's playable areas combined.</strong> Reported by Edge magazine in October.</li>
    <li><strong>Vice City is about twice Los Santos</strong>, and the map isn't drawn one-to-one with real-world Florida.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Those don't all fit together: three times RDR2 and the three-games-combined figure both imply a much bigger map than twice GTA V. They're most likely counting different things, such as water, swamp, interiors or explorable space.</p>

  <h2>Why sites quote such different numbers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Water or not.</strong> Leonida is surrounded by bays, keys and shallows. Count the water and the "map" is far bigger than the land.</li>
    <li><strong>Swamp.</strong> Grassrivers is marsh. One community measurement goes from 84 to 108 km² just by counting it as land.</li>
    <li><strong>GTA V's own size is disputed.</strong> Measured land is about 50 km², but the much-quoted 75.8 km² figure probably includes water. Use that as the baseline and GTA 6 looks only about 10% bigger.</li>
    <li><strong>Older map versions.</strong> 2024 estimates of 125 km² came from early versions of the community map, which later shrank as more trailer frames were matched.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we measured it</h2>
  <p>We took the YANIS v18 community map tiles from gtadb.org at a scale of 2 game units per pixel (one unit is roughly one metre in Rockstar's engine). We then counted every pixel that isn't sea, lake or shallow water. That gives {LAND_KM2} km², close to independent community measurements of 83.8 and 85.6 km². It's only as accurate as the community map, so we'll re-measure once the real game has been mapped.</p>

  <h2>Explore it yourself</h2>
  <p>Zoom into every region on the <a href="/gta-6/map/">interactive GTA 6 map</a>, or read up on <a href="/gta-6/heists/">heists in GTA 6</a>.</p>

  <script define:vars={{ MAPS }} is:inline>
    (() => {
      const boxes = [...document.querySelectorAll("#size-tool input[type=checkbox]")];
      const stage = document.getElementById("size-squares"), rows = document.getElementById("size-rows");
      const gta6 = MAPS.find((m) => m.id === "gta6");
      const render = () => {
        const picked = MAPS.filter((m) => boxes.find((b) => b.value === m.id)?.checked).sort((a, b) => b.km2 - a.km2);
        const max = Math.max(...picked.map((m) => m.km2), 1);
        stage.innerHTML = picked.map((m) => {
          const pct = Math.sqrt(m.km2 / max) * 100;
          return `<div class="size-sq" style="width:${pct}%;height:${pct}%;--c:${m.color}"><span>${m.name}</span></div>`;
        }).join("");
        rows.innerHTML = picked.map((m) => `<tr><td><span class="size-dot" style="--c:${m.color}"></span>${m.name}<br><small>${m.note}</small></td><td class="num">${m.km2} km²</td><td class="num">${m.id === "gta6" ? "-" : (gta6.km2 / m.km2).toFixed(2) + "×"}</td></tr>`).join("");
      };
      boxes.forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("change", render));
      render();
    })();
  </script>
  <style>
    .size-picks { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 16px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
    .size-pick { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; cursor: pointer; font-size: .92rem; }
    .size-pick span::before, .size-dot { content: ""; display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--c); margin-right: 6px; }
    .size-stage { position: relative; width: min(100%, 420px); aspect-ratio: 1; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
    .size-squares { position: absolute; inset: 0; }
    :global(.size-sq) { position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0; border: 2px solid var(--c); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--c) 18%, transparent); border-radius: 6px; }
    :global(.size-sq span) { position: absolute; top: 4px; right: 6px; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--c); text-align: right; max-width: 90%; }
  </style>
</Article>
